SIOSET - SIO speed settings››Syntax:› SIOSET [unit] [type [usindex]]› SIOSET REFRESH [0|128]› SIOSET WAITACK [[$]value]››Shows or changes how the SIO driver›talks to each drive. Settings are›normally found on the first access: a›drive that answers the Ultra Speed›question is used at its speed (US),›else one that takes the XF551's high›speed commands is used with them (XF),›else the standard speed. SIOSET alone›lists all drives; SIOSET n shows drive›n. Unit 0 means all drives.››Types:› RESET   forget; detect on next use› NORMAL  standard speed› XF      XF551 protocol› INDUS   Indus GT protocol› US      Ultra Speed; finds the speed,›         or uses usindex if given››REFRESH 128 makes the driver ask a›drive again on its next use after a›transfer failed; 0 (the default) does›not.››WAITACK sets the time to wait for a›drive's answer (EOS waits WAITACK x 2›frames): 2 is the OS value, 16 is›needed for SIO2BT. REFRESH and WAITACK›keep their values until the computer›is switched off.››After DEVICE SIO /A or /C in›CONFIG.SYS only the OS's SIO is used›and SIOSET answers 154.››In Altirra the standard emulated drive›takes the XF551's commands, so drives›show XF; the SIO patch is faster than›any real speed there: SIOSET n NORMAL›for a drive, or DEVICE SIO /A for all,›keeps it in use.››Examples:› SIOSET› SIOSET 8 US› SIOSET WAITACK 16››See also: MAP, DF›